cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AlienBody: Diagnosing How LLM Agents Acquire and Use Action Models"
message: "If you use this software / benchmark, please cite the camera-ready paper once available."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous authors"
    affiliation: "Under peer review"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnonymousPubCode/ICLR27-AlienBody"
abstract: >-
  AlienBody is a 900-instance diagnostic benchmark that randomizes action
  mappings to separate exploration, interpretation, and planning. Controlled
  naming, rule-definition, and interface interventions make acquisition and
  use of action models separately measurable for LLM agents.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - action models
  - anonymous actions
  - diagnostic benchmark
